CM_ "Application CAN Version: 1908_01";
CM_ BO_ 2499756105 "This Message is the only message that is required for the XPAND System to operate. See individual signal comments and the Integration Guide.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_State_ReqMode "A signal from the Application that requests that the Battery Management System enter Charge/Discharge Mode.
This only works if Contactor_Command is Close & APP_Comm_RollingCount is incrementing.
See Value Descriptions";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_Contactor_Command "A signal from the Application that requests that the Battery Management System closes contactors.
This only works if App_StateReqMode is Charge/Discharge & APP_Comm_RollingCount is incrementing.
See Value Descriptions";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_Balancing_Enable_F "Signal from the Application that communicates to the Battery Management System that Cell Balance (if neccessary) is allowed.
See Value Descriptions tab for more information.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_Comm_RollingCount "An incrementing signal from the Application that the Battery Management System used to calculate freshness.
The Application should increment (with rollover) this signal every time it's message is transmitted to the Battery Management System.

";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_IsoRes_Enable_F "CURRENTLY NOT SUPPORTED.  Signal from the Application that communicates to the Battery Management System that Runtime Isolation Detection is allowed.
See Value Descriptions tab for more information.";
CM_ BO_ 2499756132 "These signals communicate the state of the Battery Management System.  Look here for an overal understanding of the state of the BMS.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Comm_StringsAddressed "This signal communicates the number of strings addressed at initialization";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Contactor_EmergencyOpen_F "This signal communicates if there was a Battery Management Fault that necessitated the contactors opening immediately.  If this happens, there will be a Fault flag set in BATT_Diagnostics
";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_HVIL_Status "This signal communicates the high level status of the HVIL.   See the Value Description";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Balancing_Status "This signal communicates if a string in the BMS is currently balancing. See the Value Description";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_State_SysPwrMd "This signal communicates the overal state of the System. When in Partial Run or Run, one or more strings are connected to High Voltage.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Contactor_StringsConnected "This signal communicates the number of strings connected to High Voltage at any given time.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Comm_RollingCount "An ever incrementing signal that the Application can chose to monitor to ensure the BMS is sending fresh information with each message.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_IsoRes_Source "The results of the Isolation Test can be recovered from NVM or it can be from recently running the Isolation Test.  This signal communicates the source of the results.";
